{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":3,"query":"name=Christensen&limit=10&title=The Innovator's Solution","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"innovator's solution","subTitle":"creating and sustaining successful growth"},"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Christensen, Clayton M.",{"@type":"date","#text":"1952-2020"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Raynor, Michael"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Boston, Mass"}}],"publisher":"Harvard Business School Press","dateIssued":["c2003",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2003"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"x, 304 p. : ill. ; 24 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"In his worldwide bestseller The Innovator's Dilemma, Christensen explained how industry leaders get blindsided by disruptive innovations precisely because they focus too closely on their most profitable customers and businesses. The Innovator's Solution shows how companies get to the side of this dilemma, creating disruptions rather than being destroyed by them.\" \"Drawing on years of in-depth research and illustrated by company examples across many industries, Christensen and Raynor argue that innovation can be a predictable process that delivers sustainable, profitable growth. They identify the forces that cause managers to make bad decisions as they package and shape new ideas - and offer new frameworks to help managers create the right conditions, at the right time, for a disruption to succeed.\" \"Revealing counterintuitive insights that will change your perspective on innovation forever, this landmark book shows how to create a disruptive growth engine that fuels ongoing success.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"tableOfContents":"How to succeed at the mandate to grow -- How can we beat our most powerful competitors? -- What products will customers want to buy? -- Who are the best customers for our products? -- Getting the scope of the business right -- How to avoid commoditization -- Is your organization capable of disruptive growth? -- Managing the strategy development process -- There is good money, and there is bad money.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Clayton M. Christensen, Michael E. Raynor."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Creative ability in business"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Industrial management"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Customer services"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Success in business"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD53 .C493 2003"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"658.4063"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1578518520 (hardcover : alk. paper)"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"59308801"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990092073620203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD53 .C54 2003"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD53 .C54 2003"},{"physicalLocation"